    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "R, S",
      "explanation": "For multiplexer P, $Y=I_0\\bar S+I_1S=\\bar a\\bar b+0\\cdot b$. For mux Q, $Y=\\bar a\\bar b+\\bar b\\cdot b=\\bar a\\bar b$. For mux R, $Y=\\bar b\\cdot\\bar b+\\bar a\\cdot b=\\bar a+\\bar b=(ab)'$. For mux S, $Y=1\\cdot\\bar a+\\bar b\\cdot a=\\bar a+\\bar b=(ab)'$. So, R, S implement NAND gate P, Q implements NOR gate.",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
